
Practical 10: NumPy_Arrays
Objective: Demonstrate NumPy array creation, indexing, slicing, reshaping, broadcasting and mathematical operations on multidimensional arrays.

Subject: Python for Data Science (BE05000231)

Note: Run the cells from top to bottom. This notebook is written in a simple practical/lab style.


!pip install numpy
     

import numpy as np

arr = np.array([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]])
print(arr)
print("Shape:", arr.shape)
print("Dimensions:", arr.ndim)
     
Indexing and slicing

print("Element:", arr[0, 1])
print("First row:", arr[0])
print("First two columns:")
print(arr[:, :2])
     
Reshaping

a = np.arange(1, 13)
print("Original:", a)
print("Reshaped:")
print(a.reshape(3, 4))
     
Broadcasting

a = np.array([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]])
print(a + 10)
print(a * 2)
     
Mathematical operations

a = np.array([10, 20, 30, 40])
print("Sum:", np.sum(a))
print("Mean:", np.mean(a))
print("Square root:", np.sqrt(a))
print("Maximum:", np.max(a))
print("Minimum:", np.min(a))
     
